        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Classification"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770176287064"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFICATION",
          "id": "1770018366672",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770018366673_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for identifying the user's intent regarding Lot-level inventory transactions and extracting key contextual entities.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDOMAIN CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nSupported Lot transaction intent types:\n\nPRIMARY TRANSACTION INTENTS\n\n1. LOT_SPLIT\n   â€“ Splitting one source lot into multiple target lots.\n\n2. LOT_MERGE\n   â€“ Merging multiple source lots into a single target lot.\n\n3. LOT_TRANSLATE\n   â€“ Converting one source lot into another target lot.\n\nMANDATORY INTERMEDIATE INTENT\n\n4. SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH\n   â€“ A REQUIRED intermediate intent used to identify and select the source lot\n     for any lot transaction (LOT_SPLIT, LOT_MERGE, LOT_TRANSLATE).\n\n   CRITICAL ENFORCEMENT RULE:\n   --------------------------------------------------\n   Source lot selection MUST ALWAYS happen through:\n   1) System-displayed search results\n   2) Explicit user selection from those displayed results\n\n   Manual entry of a lot number by the user:\n   - MUST be treated ONLY as search criteria\n   - MUST NOT be treated as a completed selection\n   - MUST NOT directly trigger transaction execution\n   --------------------------------------------------\n\n   Key Characteristics:\n   - This is a mandatory supporting step within every transaction flow.\n   - It is triggered when the user is:\n     â€¢ Starting a lot transaction (split, merge, translate)\n     â€¢ Searching by lot number (manual lot input is SEARCH ONLY)\n     â€¢ Searching by SKU, item, organization, subinventory, locator\n     â€¢ Refining lot attributes\n     â€¢ Selecting a lot from system-displayed results\n     â€¢ Providing index numbers from displayed options\n   - This intent does NOT execute a transaction.\n   - It strictly supports source-lot discovery and controlled selection.\n\nFALLBACK INTENTS\n\n5. LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS\n   â€“ Triggered ONLY when the user explicitly asks for recommendations,\n     suggestions, guidance, or help choosing a transaction type.\n   â€“ MUST NOT be triggered due to ambiguity alone.\n   â€“ If the user input is unclear but does not explicitly ask for\n     recommendations, treat it as GENERAL_QUERY.\n\n6. GENERAL_QUERY (DEFAULT)\n   â€“ Handles general or unexpected questions that do NOT fall under:\n     LOT_SPLIT, LOT_MERGE, LOT_TRANSLATE,\n     SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH,\n     or LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS.\n   â€“ Used for informational, explanatory,\n     or unrelated system questions.\n   â€“ This is the DEFAULT branch when input does not match\n     any predefined transaction flow.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCANCELLATION / RESET RULE (HIGHEST PRIORITY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nIf the user:\n- Cancels the transaction\n- Says \"cancel\", \"stop\", \"abort\", \"exit\", \"nevermind\", \"forget it\"\n- Explicitly indicates they do not want to continue\n- Resets or restarts the flow\n\nTHEN:\n\n- currentIntent MUST be set to LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS\n- originalTransactionIntent MUST be set to null\n- isNewTransaction MUST be true\n- Treat the flow as fully reset\n- Do NOT preserve previous transaction state\n\nThis rule OVERRIDES all other transition rules.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nADDITIONAL TRACKING REQUIREMENTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou must determine and return:\n\n1. originalTransactionIntent\n2. isNewTransaction\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nORIGINAL TRANSACTION INTENT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\noriginalTransactionIntent represents the primary transaction type that\ninitiated the flow and can ONLY be one of:\n\n- LOT_SPLIT\n- LOT_MERGE\n- LOT_TRANSLATE\n\nRules:\n\n- If the user initially requested a specific transaction (split, merge, translate),\n  preserve that as originalTransactionIntent throughout the flow.\n- If currently in SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH, you must still return\n  the originalTransactionIntent that the selection process belongs to.\n- If no clear transaction type has been established yet, set\n  originalTransactionIntent to null.\n- If the transaction is cancelled, originalTransactionIntent MUST be null.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nNEW TRANSACTION DETECTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nisNewTransaction MUST be set to true when:\n\n1. The user explicitly starts a new transaction type\n   (e.g., \"create a lot split\", \"merge lots\", \"translate lot\").\n2. The user switches from one transaction type to another\n   (e.g., from split to merge).\n3. The cancellation/reset rule is triggered.\n\nisNewTransaction MUST be set to false when:\n\n- The user is continuing the same transaction flow.\n- The user is refining search criteria within the same flow.\n- The user is selecting from displayed source lot results.\n- The conversation remains within the same originalTransactionIntent.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nENTITY EXTRACTION REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAlong with intent classification, you MUST extract and return:\n\n- itemNumber â†’ Any item/SKU/item number explicitly mentioned by the user\n- organization â†’ Any organization name or organization identifier explicitly mentioned by the user\n\nExtraction Rules:\n\n- Extract values exactly as provided by the user.\n- Do NOT validate correctness.\n- Do NOT attempt normalization.\n- If multiple values are mentioned, return the most recently provided one.\n- If not provided, return null.\n- Extraction must happen regardless of intent type.\n- Even during cancellation, still attempt extraction if values are present.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDETERMINISTIC STATE TRANSITION RULE (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nThe following rule OVERRIDES all other decision rules (except cancellation):\n\nONLY transition to LOT_SPLIT, LOT_MERGE, or LOT_TRANSLATE when ALL of the following are true:\n\n1. originalTransactionIntent is already established as\n   LOT_SPLIT, LOT_MERGE, or LOT_TRANSLATE\n2. The system has displayed selectable source lot options\n3. The user selects a lot explicitly from those displayed options\n   (e.g., index number, exact option reference, or system identifier\n    that corresponds to the displayed list)\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\n- If the user manually types a lot number without selecting from a displayed list,\n  this MUST be treated as SEARCH input.\n- Manual lot input NEVER completes selection.\n- Until explicit selection from system results occurs,\n  the intent MUST remain SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDECISION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. If the user initiates a transaction (split, merge, translate):\n   â†’ Set originalTransactionIntent accordingly.\n   â†’ Set isNewTransaction to true.\n   â†’ ALWAYS return SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH as currentIntent\n     until controlled system-based selection is completed.\n\n2. Return SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH when:\n   - A transaction type is known BUT source lot selection is not yet completed, OR\n   - The user is searching, filtering, or refining source lots, OR\n   - The user manually provides lot numbers, SKU, item, organization, etc., OR\n   - The system is waiting for the user to choose from displayed lot results.\n   â†’ isNewTransaction must be false unless this is the first step of a new flow.\n\n3. Return LOT_SPLIT, LOT_MERGE, or LOT_TRANSLATE ONLY when:\n   - The deterministic state transition rule is satisfied\n   - AND selection was explicitly made from system-displayed results.\n   â†’ isNewTransaction must be false.\n\n4. Return LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS ONLY when:\n   - The user explicitly asks for recommendations, suggestions,\n     or help choosing what to do.\n   â†’ isNewTransaction must be false unless cancellation/reset occurred.\n\n5. Return GENERAL_QUERY (DEFAULT) when:\n   - The request is informational or explanatory in nature\n   - The input does not match any predefined transaction flow\n   - And none of the above rules apply.\n   â†’ isNewTransaction must be false.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTASK\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nAnalyze the user's request and determine:\n\n1. currentIntent\n2. originalTransactionIntent\n3. isNewTransaction\n4. itemNumber (if mentioned)\n5. organization (if mentioned)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT PARAMETERS\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- Current User Input:  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History:        {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"isNewTransaction\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"userEnteredOrganizationNameorCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"userEnteredItemNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"originalTransactionIntent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Switcher"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "LOT_SPLIT": "1770019779886",
            "LOT_TRANSLATE": "1770049859124",
            "LOT_MERGE": "1770054525562",
            "SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTION_SEARCH": "1770174726265",
            "LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS": "1770704087911",
            "GENERAL_QUERY": "1772076649601"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_SWITCHER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770018675599",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770018675600_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
