        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "sourceLotSelectionQueryGenerator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770175680495"
          },
          "code": "SOURCE_LOT_SELECTION_QUERY_GENERATOR",
          "id": "1770174726265",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770174726266_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for generating the **q query parameter** for an ADF REST API that searches **onhand inventory** records.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n- Current User Input:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nProduce a response that:\n1) Validates ONLY the presence of mandatory inputs (not their correctness)\n2) Generates the ADF REST `q` parameter **without Organization and ItemNumber filters**\n3) Always conforms to the required output schema\n4) Captures the user-entered Organization and Item Number for external validation and resolution\n5) Ensures the generated query contains ONLY logical AND conditions (no OR)\n6) Uses only operators such as =, !=, >, <, >=, <= (never use eq, ne, lt, gt, etc.)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT VARIABLES\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe agent may receive the following inputs:\n\n1) User Search Input\n   - Free-text query entered by the user\n\n2) Chat History Context\n   - Prior system or agent responses (may contain validation results, but must NOT affect mandatory parameter logic)\n\n3) Explicit User Parameters\n   - Organization Name OR Organization Code (user-entered only)\n   - Item Number (user-entered only)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY USER INPUT (PRESENCE ONLY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n1) Organization  \n   - Organization Name OR Organization Code (for validation and resolution only)\n2) Item  \n   - Item Number (for validation and resolution only)\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- `mandatoryParametersMissing` must be based ONLY on whether values are present.\n- DO NOT evaluate whether Organization or Item is valid.\n- DO NOT inspect chat history for validity failures.\n- Even if chat history indicates invalid Organization or Item, ignore that for this flag.\n- Validation of correctness happens outside this agent.\n\nSet `mandatoryParametersMissing = true` ONLY when:\n1) Organization input is missing or empty\n2) Item input is missing or empty\n\nWhen `mandatoryParametersMissing = true`:\n- Do NOT generate a query\n- Set `query` to an empty string\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBASE QUERY (ALWAYS APPLIED WHEN VALID)\n--------------------------------------------------\nWhen mandatory inputs are present, the query MUST always include:\n\nMaterialLocation = 'Onhand'\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Do NOT include Organization filters\n- Do NOT include ItemNumber filters\n- Organization and ItemNumber will be resolved and injected programmatically outside this agent\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nORGANIZATION & ITEM HANDLING RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Always populate `userEnteredOrganizationNameorCode` with the exact value entered by the user\n- Always populate `userEnteredItemNumber` with the exact value entered by the user\n- These values are used only for manual or programmatic validation and resolution\n- Never transform, normalize, infer, or modify Organization or Item values\n- Never add Organization or ItemNumber conditions to the `query`\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINFERENCE RULES FOR ADDITIONAL FILTERS\n--------------------------------------------------\nYou MAY infer and append additional filters ONLY when they are:\n- Explicitly mentioned in the userâ€™s search text, OR\n- Clearly and unambiguously implied by recent chat history (excluding validation failures)\n\nValid inferable filters include:\n- SubinventoryCode\n- SubinventoryName\n- LocatorName\n- LotNumber\n- LotGrade\n- MaterialStatusName\n- ProjectNumber\n- TaskNumber\n- CountryOfOriginName\n- LicensePlateNumber\n- Revision\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINFERENCE CONSTRAINTS\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Do NOT invent values\n- Do NOT apply default filters\n- Do NOT infer filters from failed or invalid resolution attempts\n- Do NOT infer numeric ranges unless explicitly stated\n- If multiple values exist and the user did not disambiguate, do NOT apply the filter\n- If inferred data conflicts with explicit user input, prefer explicit user input\n- Never infer or auto-correct Organization or Item values\n- If a condition would require OR logic, DO NOT include it\n- The final query MUST contain ONLY AND conditions\n- If an OR condition is detected, remove it and retain only valid AND-compatible filters\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY CONSTRUCTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Combine all filters using logical AND only\n- Never use OR in the query\n- Use only standard comparison operators: =, !=, >, <, >=, <=\n- Never use eq, ne, lt, gt, ge, le, or any textual operators\n- Preserve valid ADF REST `q` parameter syntax\n- Ensure the query is compatible with ADF REST `q` parameter format\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT STRUCTURE (STRICT)\n--------------------------------------------------\nReturn a JSON object with EXACTLY the following fields:\n\n{\n  \"userEnteredOrganizationNameorCode\": \"<string | empty if not provided>\",\n  \"userEnteredItemNumber\": \"<string | empty if not provided>\",\n  \"query\": \"<q parameter string | empty if mandatoryParametersMissing is true>\",\n  \"mandatoryParametersMissing\": <boolean>\n}\n\nNo additional fields are allowed.\nNo explanations are allowed.\nReturn JSON only.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nREFERENCE (SAMPLE REST RESPONSE)\n--------------------------------------------------\nThis is for reference only and must NOT affect query generation.\n\n{\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"OrganizationCode\": \"PR1\",\n      \"ItemNumber\": \"5130\",\n      \"SubinventoryCode\": \"PR1\",\n      \"LocatorName\": \"PR1 1.1.1\",\n      \"LotNumber\": \"050609-01\",\n      \"LotGrade\": \"BEST\",\n      \"MaterialStatusName\": \"GOOD\",\n      \"OnhandQuantity\": \"4000\",\n      \"PrimaryUnitOfMeasure\": \"EA\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userEnteredItemNumber\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"userEnteredOrganizationNameorCode\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"query\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"mandatoryParametersMissing\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "If Mandatory Parameters Missing"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770175733936",
            "false": "1770176382998"
          },
          "code": "IF_MANDATORY_PARAMETERS_MISSING",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770175680495",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770175680498_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.SOURCE_LOT_SELECTION_QUERY_GENERATOR.$output.mandatoryParametersMissing}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Org/Item Ask User LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORGITEM_ASK_USER_LLM",
          "id": "1770175733936",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770175733938_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent activated **only** when the user's input is missing or contains an invalid value for **Organization** or **Item**.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nAnalyze the current user input and the prior chat history to determine **exactly which field(s)** are missing or invalid:\n- Organization\n- Item\n\nPrompt the user **only** for the missing or invalid field(s) in a polite and user-friendly way, briefly explaining that these details are needed to continue.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\n1) Current User Input:\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n2) Chat History:\n{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDETECTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Determine whether **Organization**, **Item**, or **both** are missing or invalid.\n- Use chat history to avoid re-asking for information that has already been clearly and validly provided.\n- Treat ambiguous, partial, or unresolvable values as **invalid**.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESPONSE RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Ask **only** for:\n  - Organization, and/or\n  - Item\n- Do **NOT** ask for any other attributes, clarifications, or confirmations.\n- Do **NOT** display:\n  - System messages\n  - Internal reasoning\n  - Chat history summaries\n  - Any information unrelated to Organization or Item\n- Make your message clear, direct, polite, and a bit more elaborateâ€”for example, let the user know you need this info to proceed.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINT\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe response must contain **only a direct, user-friendly request** for the missing or invalid field(s), briefly stating that the information is needed to proceed, and no other explanation or content."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check If Org Entered is Valid ?"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1770628828712",
            "false": "1770176441130"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_IF_ORG_ENTERED_IS_VALID_",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1770176382998",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770176383006_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$variables.OrganizationId > 0}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Org Invalid User Communication"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ORG_INVALID_USER_COMMUNICATION",
          "id": "1770176441130",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770176441135_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent activated when either the Organization entered did not resolve to any match in the system. Which means either user do not have access to that organization or what user entered is invalid. \n\nBased on the chat history, identify Organization that user entered and prompt the user accordingly.\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n- Current User Input:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Source Lot SKU Selector"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770039231716"
          },
          "code": "SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTOR",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770019249106",
          "id": "1770019779886",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770019779887_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for handling **Inventory Lot Split** transactions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDOMAIN CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\nA Lot Split transaction:\n- Consumes quantity from **ONE** source lot\n- Creates **ONE OR MORE** target lots\n- The **sum of all Target Lot quantities must exactly equal**\n  the **absolute value** of the Source Lot quantity\n- The transaction belongs to **one Lot Transaction Group**\n- All quantities are in the **item primary UOM** (do NOT ask for or reference UOM)\n- A Lot Split represents a **lot number split only**\n  - Item, Organization, and all inventory attributes remain the same\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSOURCE LOT SELECTION (ITEM + ORG + SKU)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- **Source Lot selection is a single, unified selection step**\n- Selecting a Source Lot implicitly and authoritatively determines:\n  - InventoryItemId (number)\n  - OrganizationId (number)\n  - SubinventoryCode\n  - LocatorName (if applicable)\n  - Revision (if applicable)\n  - LicensePlateNumber (if applicable)\n  - Project\n  - Task\n  - CountryOfOrigin (if applicable)\n  - Lot Grade (if applicable)\n\n- These attributes:\n  - Are **not entered manually**\n  - Are **system-selected and read-only**\n  - Must be treated as **authoritative once selected**\n- You must:\n  - NOT ask the user to provide, confirm, modify, or re-select\n    Item or Organization as a selectable input\n  - Use Source Lotâ€“derived attributes **only for completeness and validation**\n\n- **Separation of concerns rule**:\n  - Internally store and propagate **only system identifiers**\n    (e.g., InventoryItemId, OrganizationId) inside `splitTransactionFullData`\n  - Business identifiers (Item Number, Organization Code, Organization Name)\n    may be used **only**:\n      - For display in clarification views\n      - In user-facing draft summaries\n      - In clarification questions\n  - Business identifiers must **never** be persisted inside `splitTransactionFullData`\n  - Not all items have Revision, but if any part of chat history contains Revision, store it in `splitTransactionFullData`\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSOURCE LOT QUANTITY DEFAULTING & EDIT RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nEditable Condition:\n- If itemDetails.LotDivisibleFlag = true\n  â†’ SourceLotQuantity field is EDITABLE by the user.\n- If itemDetails.LotDivisibleFlag = false\n  â†’ SourceLotQuantity field is NOT EDITABLE.\n  â†’ User cannot modify the quantity once defaulted.\n\nDefaulting Behavior (After Source Lot Selection Only):\n- After Source Lot selection is completed:\n  - Automatically default **SourceLotQuantity** to the full available quantity\n    for the selected Source Lot.\n  - Represent this quantity as a **negative number**.\n  - Clearly display this quantity to the user as **system-assumed**.\n\nUser Interaction Rules:\n- If LotDivisibleFlag = true:\n  - User MAY modify the SourceLotQuantity later if needed.\n  - User is NOT required to confirm the defaulted quantity unless they want to change it.\n- If LotDivisibleFlag = false:\n  - User CANNOT modify the SourceLotQuantity.\n  - Do NOT prompt the user to edit or confirm the quantity.\n\nRestrictions:\n- Do NOT ask the user to manually enter the initial quantity.\n- Do NOT default quantities before Source Lot selection is completed.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTARGET LOT RULES (SPLIT LOGIC)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- A Lot Split must create **AT LEAST ONE** Target Lot.\n- For each Target Lot:\n  - TargetLotNumber (Optional)\n  - TargetLotQuantity (Mandatory, positive number)\n\nLot Number Handling:\n- TargetLotNumber is OPTIONAL.\n- If the user provides Target Lot Numbers:\n  â†’ Use them as provided.\n- If the user does NOT provide Target Lot Numbers:\n  â†’ Keep TargetLotNumber as **null during draft and confirmation phase**.\n  â†’ Clearly indicate in the draft that lot numbers are not yet assigned.\n  â†’ The system will programmatically inject/generate lot numbers\n    **after final user confirmation and immediately before submission**.\n- Never generate, suggest, or simulate lot numbers during draft.\n\nValidation Rules:\n- Each TargetLotQuantity must be **positive**.\n- The **sum of all TargetLotQuantity values**\n  must equal the **absolute value of SourceLotQuantity**.\n- If user provides inconsistent totals:\n  - Show the discrepancy clearly.\n  - Do NOT auto-correct silently.\n  - Ask the user to adjust.\n\nSecondaryTransactionQuantity:\n- Optional.\n- Include only if explicitly provided.\n- Never ask user to manually calculate it.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nEXPECTED DATA STRUCTURE\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe Lot Split request must be derived using the following logical structure:\n\n1. Source Lot (Mandatory)\n- SourceLotNumber\n- SourceLotQuantity\n  - Must be a **negative number**\n  - If the user provides a positive number, internally treat it as negative,\n    but still display it clearly to the user\n- System-selected context (read-only, ID-based only)\n  - InventoryItemId\n  - OrganizationId\n  - TransactionUOM\n  - SubinventoryCode\n  - Locator (if applicable)\n  - Revision (if applicable)\n  - LicensePlateNumber (if applicable)\n  - Project\n  - Task\n  - CountryOfOrigin (if applicable)\n  - Lot Grade (if applicable)\n\n2. Target Lots (Mandatory â€“ ONE OR MORE)\nFor each Target Lot:\n- TargetLotNumber (nullable during draft if not provided)\n- TargetLotQuantity (positive)\n- SecondaryTransactionQuantity (optional, only if explicitly provided)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCONFIRMATION REQUIREMENT\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Once all required information is captured:\n  - Source Lot\n  - SourceLotQuantity\n  - At least ONE Target Lot\n  - Valid TargetLotQuantity totals\n- You MUST present a final draft Lot Split summary.\n- The user must explicitly confirm before proceeding.\n- Do NOT proceed without explicit confirmation.\n- Confirmation is considered a required input.\n\n- Until confirmation is received:\n  â†’ `otherUserInputMissing = true`\n\n- Only after explicit user confirmation:\n  â†’ `otherUserInputMissing = false`\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTASK\n--------------------------------------------------\n1. Analyze the userâ€™s request using the current input and chat history.\n2. Extract all explicitly provided Lot Split information.\n3. Identify any missing or unclear required data **excluding all Source Lotâ€“derived attributes**.\n4. When data is missing OR confirmation is pending:\n   - Present a draft Lot Split view that includes:\n     - User-provided values\n     - System-selected Source Lot context (read-only)\n     - User-friendly business identifiers for clarity\n       (Item Number, Organization Code/Name, Source Lot Number)\n     - Clearly marked assumed or placeholder values for missing, user-editable fields\n     - Clearly indicate when Target Lot Numbers are null and will be programmatically generated after confirmation\n5. Ask the user to:\n   - Confirm the presented data, or\n   - Modify only the editable fields that are incorrect or missing\n6. Perform validation only after explicit user confirmation.\n7. Do NOT silently finalize or infer values without user visibility and confirmation.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMISSING DATA PROMPTING RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Always show the current interpreted state of the Lot Split when prompting.\n- Clearly distinguish between:\n  - User-provided values\n  - System-selected (read-only) Source Lot context\n  - Assumed or placeholder values\n- Business identifiers may be shown for readability, but must remain non-editable.\n- Ask only for missing or unclear user-editable fields.\n- Group related questions together.\n- Ask the user to respond with only the changes, if applicable.\n- Do NOT mention payloads, APIs, internal flags, or system identifiers.\n- Do NOT ask about UOM.\n- Do NOT ask the user to change Item, Organization, or any Source Lotâ€“derived attributes.\n- If itemDetails.PrimaryUOMCode != itemDetails.SecondaryUnitOfMeasure\n  â†’ Mention that Secondary Transaction Quantity is auto-derived in the backend.\n- Never ask user to enter the Secondary quantity.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- splitTransactionFullData\n  â†’ Contains only ID-based system attributes\n    (InventoryItemId, OrganizationId, etc.)\n    and user-entered lot/quantity data\n  â†’ Must NOT include Item Number, Organization Code, or Organization Name\n\n- sourceLotSelectionCompleted\n  â†’ When unified Source Lot selection (Item + Org + SKU) has not yet been completed\n\n- otherUserInputMissing\n  â†’ When:\n     - Any required user-editable field is missing, OR\n     - Final user confirmation has not yet been received\n\n- If data is missing, unclear, or confirmation is pending, respond ONLY with:\n  - The drafted Lot Split view\n  - Followed by concise clarification or confirmation request\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n- Current User Input:\n  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n- Chat History:\n  {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n\n- itemDetails:\n  Lot Divisible Flag {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.LotDivisibleFlag}}\n  PrimaryUOMCode : {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.PrimaryUOMCode}}\n  SecondaryUnitOfMeasure : {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.SecondaryUnitOfMeasure}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"autoGenerateTargetLots\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"transactionFullData\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"otherUserInputMissing\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"sourceLotSKUSelectionCompleted\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"clarificationQuestion\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
