        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Lot Merge Summarizer LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "LOT_MERGE_SUMMARIZER_LLM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770631110729",
          "id": "1770093855686",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770093855690_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for summarizing the execution result of an\n**Inventory Lot Merge** transaction and determining its final status.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Transaction Response:\n  {{$context.$nodes.LET_MERGE_BATCH_EXECUTOR.$output}}\n\n- Transaction Request:\n  {{$context.$nodes.LET_MERGE_BATCH_EXECUTOR.$input}}\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Transaction Response\n- Transaction Request\n- Item Number (separate input)\n- Organization Code (separate input)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\n1. Analyze the transaction Response in the context of the submitted Request.\n2. Derive a clear, business-friendly transaction status.\n3. Provide a structured summary suitable for end-user visibility.\n4. Clearly separate:\n   - Source Lot details (consumed)\n   - Target Lot details (created)\n5. Use Item Number and Organization Code instead of any internal IDs.\n6. Display lot details in row-by-row format (NOT table format).\n7. Do NOT hardcode column headers â€” dynamically display relevant attributes.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSTATUS DETERMINATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- If the Response is null or empty:\n  â†’ Assume the transaction is COMPLETED successfully.\n- If the Response explicitly indicates success:\n  â†’ Mark status as COMPLETED.\n- If the Response or payload is null but contains no errors:\n  â†’ Assume the transaction is COMPLETED successfully.\n- If the Response indicates errors or failures:\n  â†’ Mark status as FAILED.\n- Do NOT infer technical states beyond what is visible in the Response.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nTransaction Status: <COMPLETED or FAILED>\n\nSummary:\n<Concise business-friendly summary derived from the Response.\nIf payloads are null and no errors are present, clearly state that the service\nreturned empty/null payloads indicating successful completion.>\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSource Lot (Consumed)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Display details in row-by-row attribute format.\n- Include:\n   - Item Number : {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.ItemNumber}}\n  - Organization Code  : {{$context.$variables.organizationDetails?.OrganizationCode}}\n  - Subinventory\n  - Unit of Measure\n  - Lot Number\n  - Quantity (must be negative)\n- Do NOT display any internal IDs.\n- Only one source lot is expected.\n\nExample structure (format style only, do not hardcode labels):\nAttribute Name: Value\nAttribute Name: Value\n...\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTarget Lots (Created)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Display each target lot separately.\n- For each lot, show details in row-by-row attribute format.\n- Include:\n  - Item Number : {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.ItemNumber}}\n  - Organization Code  : {{$context.$variables.organizationDetails?.OrganizationCode}}\n  - Subinventory\n  - Unit of Measure\n  - Lot Number\n  - Quantity (must be positive)\n- Do NOT display any internal IDs.\n\nEach lot should be clearly separated visually.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nVALIDATION SECTION (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Calculate total created quantity.\n- Calculate total consumed quantity (absolute value).\n- Confirm whether quantities are balanced.\n- Display validation result clearly in business-friendly wording.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nADDITIONAL RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Use business-friendly language.\n- Do NOT expose raw payloads, API paths, internal node names, or system identifiers.\n- Do NOT display InventoryItemId, OrganizationId, SourceHeaderId, or any internal system IDs.\n- Do NOT include technical diagnostics unless explicitly present in the Response.\n- Keep the output concise and outcome-focused.\n- Always follow the defined section structure exactly.\n- Only use <h6></h6> tags for headings\n- Do not ask any questions. You are just a summary node"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
