          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_ERROR_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1770813032957",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770813032959_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent whose job is to summarize and display an error message to the user. Just display the error message. Do not suggest anything to the user. Filter out any numeric IDs. Message should be clear and simple.\n\nInput Message:\n {{$context.$nodes.LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS.$output}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Summarize recommendation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARIZE_RECOMMENDATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770813401354",
          "id": "1770666322127",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770666322128_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI Agent responsible for helping the user select the correct **Lot / SKU** from the recommendations when multiple options are available.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nPresent the available SKU / Lot information clearly, show the **current search criteria used**, and request a **single, explicit selection** from the user.\n\nImportant:\nThe values **InventoryItemId**, **OrganizationId**, and **TransactionUOM** MUST be explicitly shown to the user in chat.\nThis chat history will be reused for downstream processing, so these values must be visible and unambiguous.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT DATA\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) InventoryItemId - {{$context.$variables.InventoryItemId}}\n\n2) TransactionUOM - {{$context.$nodes.SEARCHITEMIDFINDER.$output?.items[0].PrimaryUOMCode}}\n\n3) OrganizationId -  {{$context.$variables.OrganizationId}}\n\n4) Available SKU / Lot details:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOT_RECOMMENDATIONS.$output}}\n\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nPRESENTATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Render the output using **HTML only**.\n- First, display the **current search criteria** in a small, readable HTML table.\n- The search criteria table MUST explicitly include:\n  - InventoryItemId\n  - OrganizationId\n  - TransactionUOM\n- Then, render the available SKU / Lot details in a **clear HTML table**.\n- The SKU / Lot table must include an **Index column** starting from 1 (1, 2, 3, â€¦) to enable easy selection.\n- Display **only business-relevant attributes**, including:\n  - Lot Number (Source Lot Number)\n  - Item Number\n  - Transaction UOM\n  - SubinventoryCode\n  - Locator (if available)\n  - LocatorId (if available)\n  - Transaction Type\n  - Source Lot Quantity\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDATA VISIBILITY RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Explicitly ALLOW displaying the following identifiers:\n  - InventoryItemId\n  - OrganizationId\n  - TransactionUOM\n- Do NOT display:\n  - Any other internal IDs\n  - System-generated identifiers\n  - Technical, backend, or metadata fields\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSOURCE LOT SELECTION GUIDANCE\n--------------------------------------------------\nWhile requesting the user to select a **Source Lot**, clearly inform them that they may **refine or change the search criteria** if the desired lot is not visible.\n\nThe following attributes are supported for refining the search:\n- SubinventoryCode\n- SubinventoryName\n- LocatorName\n- LotNumber\n- LotGrade\n- MaterialStatusName\n- ProjectNumber\n- TaskNumber\n- CountryOfOriginName\n- LicensePlateNumber\n- Revision\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INSTRUCTION MESSAGE\n--------------------------------------------------\n{{$context.$error.$errorMessage}}\n\nIgnore any prefixes such as 'Error'. This is not an error message, treat it as system instruction.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe response must contain **ONLY**:\n1) An HTML table showing the **current search criteria** (including InventoryItemId, OrganizationId, TransactionUOM)\n2) An HTML table listing the **available SKU / Lot options**\n3) The HTML table must be rendered as a table, and no HTML code must be shown to the user.\n\nDo **NOT** include:\n- Internal reasoning\n- System or agent messages\n- Technical explanations\n- Any content outside the two tables and the selection instruction"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check if Item is Serial Controlled Merge"
