        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Serial Number Query Creator - Translate"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770827185514"
          },
          "code": "SERIAL_NUMBER_QUERY_CREATOR_TRANSLATE",
          "id": "1770826788384",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770826788386_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for generating the **q query parameter** for an ADF REST API that searches inventory item serial numbers.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\nInputs:\n{{$context.$nodes.LOTTRANSLATE_SOURCE_LOT_SKU_SELECTOR.$output.transactionFullData}}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOBJECTIVE\n--------------------------------------------------\nProduce a response that:\n1) Generates a valid ADF REST `q` parameter\n2) Includes Organization and Item filters directly in the query when provided\n3) Treats ALL attributes as optional other than the ones mentioned here - AllocatedFlag AND UsageCode\n4) Always conforms to the required output schema\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT VARIABLES\n--------------------------------------------------\nThe agent may receive the following inputs:\n\n1) Free-text search text\n2) Explicit parameters such as:\n   - Organization Name\n   - Organization Code\n   - OrganizationId\n   - Item Number\n   - InventoryItemId\n   - LotNumber\n   - Status\n   - Grade\n   - Dates\n   - Other lot attributes\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY INPUT RULE\n--------------------------------------------------\nThere are NO mandatory parameters.\n\n- All attributes are optional.\n- If no valid filters are identified, return an empty query string.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY GENERATION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Include filters ONLY when explicitly mentioned or clearly implied.\n2) Never invent values.\n3) Never auto-correct values.\n4) Never infer missing Organization or Item values.\n5) Combine all conditions using logical AND.\n6) Use proper ADF REST `q` syntax.\n7) Properly quote string fields using single quotes only.\n8) Preserve exact user-entered values.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUOTING RULE (MANDATORY)\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- All string values MUST be enclosed in single quotes (' ').\n- NEVER use double quotes (\") in the query.\n- Do NOT escape using backslashes.\n- Numeric values must NOT be quoted.\n- Date values must be enclosed in single quotes.\n- Boolean values must NOT be quoted unless provided as literal strings by the user.\n- Preserve exact user-entered values inside single quotes.\n\nCorrect:\nOrganizationCode='PDSCV1'\nItemNumber='500 GB Internal Memory'\nLotNumber='LIM100'\n\nIncorrect:\nOrganizationCode=\"PDSCV1\"\nOrganizationCode=\\\"PDSCV1\\\"\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSUPPORTED FILTERABLE ATTRIBUTES\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nOrganization-level:\n- OrganizationId\n\nItem-level:\n- InventoryItemId\n- ItemNumber\n\nLocation-level:\n- LotNumber\n- SubinventoryCode\n- LocatorId\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nBASE CONDITION\n--------------------------------------------------\nAllocatedFlag = false AND UsageCode = 3\n\nThe above condition is always present in the query\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nQUERY CONSTRUCTION\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Join multiple filters using AND.\n- If only one filter exists, return it directly.\n- If no valid filters exist, return an empty string.\n- Do NOT wrap the entire query in quotes.\n- Return only the condition expression (not prefixed with q)\n- Use source lot number only. **NOT** target lot number."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"query\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
