        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Simplify Item Quantities Data for LLM",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const cleanItemQuantitiesLot = (data) => {\n  if (!data?.items?.length) return { items: [] };\n\n  const allowedKeys = [\n    \"OrganizationId\",\n    \"OrganizationCode\",\n    \"InventoryItemId\",\n    \"ItemNumber\",\n    \"Revision\",\n    \"SubinventoryCode\",\n    \"LocatorName\",\n    \"LotNumber\",\n    \"ProjectId\",\n    \"ProjectNumber\",\n    \"TaskId\",\n    \"TaskNumber\",\n    \"CountryOfOriginCode\",\n    \"OnhandQuantity\",\n    \"SecondaryOnhandQuantity\",\n    \"AvailableToTransact\",\n    \"LotExpirationDate\",\n    \"LicensePlateNumber\",\n    \"CountryOfOriginName\"\n  ];\n\n  const { items } = data;\n\n  const filteredItems = items.map(item => {\n    const filtered = Object.fromEntries(\n      Object.entries(item).filter(([key]) => allowedKeys.includes(key))\n    );\n\n    // âœ… Normalize AvailableToTransact (handles string, number, malformed values)\n    const value = filtered.AvailableToTransact;\n\n    if (value !== null && value !== undefined) {\n      const normalized = String(value).split(\",\")[0].trim();\n      filtered.AvailableToTransact = normalized;\n    }\n\n    return filtered;\n  });\n\n  // âœ… Remove rows where AvailableToTransact <= 0\n  const positiveQuantityItems = filteredItems.filter(item => {\n    const qty = parseFloat(item.AvailableToTransact);\n    return !isNaN(qty) && qty > 0;\n  });\n\n  // Remove columns where ALL rows are null/undefined\n  const keysToRemove = allowedKeys.filter(key =>\n    positiveQuantityItems.every(item => item[key] === null || item[key] === undefined)\n  );\n\n  const cleanedItems = positiveQuantityItems.map(item =>\n    Object.fromEntries(\n      Object.entries(item).filter(\n        ([key]) => !keysToRemove.includes(key)\n      )\n    )\n  );\n\n  return {\n    items: cleanedItems,\n    count: cleanedItems.length\n  };\n};\n\nlet itemQuantitiesLot = $context.$nodes.QUERY_ITEM_QUANTITY_LOTS.$output; \nconst cleanedData = cleanItemQuantitiesLot(itemQuantitiesLot);\n\nreturn cleanedData;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1770040056888"
          },
          "code": "SIMPLIFY_ITEM_QUANTITIES_DATA_FOR_LLM",
          "id": "1771991250484",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Lot Merge Payload Creator"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771326495104"
          },
          "code": "LOT_MERGE_TNX_PAYLOAD_CREATOR",
          "id": "1772012821863",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772012821878_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI agent responsible for creating the **Inventory Lot Merge transaction payload**.\n\nThis agent is invoked only after all required user input has been collected.\nYour sole responsibility is to construct the payload strictly from the provided input.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nDOMAIN CONTEXT\n--------------------------------------------------\nAn Inventory Lot Merge transaction follows these rules:\n\n- Quantity is consumed from TWO OR MORE source lots\n- Quantity is created into exactly ONE target (merged) lot\n- The sum of the absolute values of all source lot quantities must exactly equal the target lot quantity\n- Source and target lots belong to the same inventory item, organization, and subinventory\n- All parts must belong to the same Lot Transaction Group\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nINPUT ASSUMPTIONS\n--------------------------------------------------\n- All required data is present and complete\n- No clarification or validation is required\n- Do NOT infer, adjust, recompute, or normalize quantities or identifiers\n- Use input values exactly as provided\n- All quantities are in primary UOM (no UOM handling required)\n- If any target lot number is null or missing, use:\n  {{$context.$nodes.MERGE_GENERATE_NEW_LOT.$output}}\n  to populate the missing lot number exactly as provided\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nPAYLOAD CONSTRUCTION RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Generate ONE separate part per source lot\n- Generate ONE part for the target (merged) lot\n- Generate a unique LotTransactionGroupName (less than 30 characters) and use the same value for all parts\n- Generate a unique numeric TransactionBatchId and use the same value for all parts\n- SourceHeaderId is always 1\n- SourceLineId is always 1 for all parts\n- Skip any attribute that is null, empty, or not provided\n- All parts must share:\n  - OrganizationId\n  - InventoryItemId\n  - Revision\n  - TransactionDate\n  - LotTransactionGroupName\n  - Tracking attributes (Project / Task / Country Of Origin)\n  - Lot Grade (if applicable)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nEXPECTED DATA MODEL\n--------------------------------------------------\nCommon attributes for all parts:\n\n- TransactionTypeName = \"Inventory Lot Merge\"\n- OrganizationId (number)\n- InventoryItemId (number)\n- Revision\n- TransactionDate (use provided value below)\n- LotTransactionGroupName\n- trackingAttributesDFF\n  - projectId\n  - taskId\n  - countryOfOriginCode_Display\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSOURCE LOT PARTS (TWO OR MORE)\n--------------------------------------------------\nFor each source lot, create a separate part:\n\n- SourceLotFlag = true\n- TransactionQuantity = negative number\n- Lots array contains exactly one entry:\n  - LotNumber = source lot number\n  - TransactionQuantity = negative number (same as header)\n  - LotExpirationDate (include only if provided)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nTARGET LOT PART (Exactly ONE)\n--------------------------------------------------\n- SourceLotFlag = false\n- TransactionQuantity = positive number\n- Lots array contains exactly one entry:\n  - LotNumber = target lot number (use generated value if missing)\n  - TransactionQuantity = positive number\n  - SecondaryTransactionQuantity (include only if provided)\n  - LotExpirationDate (include only if provided)\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT RULES\n--------------------------------------------------\n- Output ONLY structured JSON\n- Do NOT include explanations, comments, or example values\n- Do NOT include validation logic or user messaging\n- Do NOT reference APIs, internal systems, or implementation details\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nOUTPUT STRUCTURE\n--------------------------------------------------\n{\n  \"parts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"<unique-part-id>\",\n      \"path\": \"/inventoryStagedTransactions\",\n      \"operation\": \"create\",\n      \"payload\": {\n        \"SourceCode\": \"SERVICE\",\n        \"ProcessStatus\": 1,\n        \"SourceHeaderId\": 1,\n        \"SourceLineId\": 1,\n        \"UseCurrentCostFlag\": \"true\",\n        \"TransactionMode\": \"1\",\n        \"TransactionBatchId\": <number>,\n        \"TransactionUnitOfMeasure\": {{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.PrimaryUOMName}},\n        \"TransactionTypeName\": \"Inventory Lot Merge\",\n        \"OrganizationId\": <organization-id (number type)>,\n        \"InventoryItemId\": {{$context.$variables.InventoryItemId}},\n        \"Revision\": \"<revision>\",\n        \"TransactionQuantity\": <number>,\n        \"TransactionDate\": \"{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\",\n        \"SubinventoryCode\": \"<subinventory-code>\",\n        \"LocatorName\": \"<locator>\",\n        \"SourceLotFlag\": <true|false>,\n        \"LotTransactionGroupName\": \"<lot-transaction-group>\",\n        \"LicensePlateNumber\": \"<lpn-id>\",\n        \"trackingAttributesDFF\": [\n          {\n            \"projectId\": \"<project-id>(number type)\",\n            \"taskId\": \"<task-id>(number type)\",\n            \"countryOfOriginCode_Display\": \"<country-of-origin>\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"lots\": [\n          {\n            \"LotNumber\": \"<lot-number>\",\n            \"TransactionQuantity\": <number>,\n            \"SecondaryTransactionQuantity\": <number (if provided)>,\n            \"LotExpirationDate\": \"<date>\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nUSER INPUT\n--------------------------------------------------\n{{$context.$nodes.LOT_MERGE_TRANSACTION_SKU_SELECTION.$output.transactionFullData}}\n\nInventory Item Id:\n{{$context.$variables.InventoryItemId}}\n\nTransaction Date:\n{{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}\n\nTransactionUnitOfMeasure:\n{{$context.$variables.itemDetails?.PrimaryUOMName}}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"payload\": {\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"properties\": {}\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
